        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TRADITIONAL DESIGN:\n  Architect makes drawing decisions directly.\n  Want to change window width: redraw windows.\n  Want to change facade rhythm: redraw facade.\n  The drawing is the final artifact."
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CONTEMPORARY.md#011",
      "path": [
        "09-CONTEMPORARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:architecture-history:09-contemporary, git-history:architecture-history:09-contemporary]",
        "canonical_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
        "concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "current_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:architecture-history:contemporary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "architecture-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "section": "architecture-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PARAMETRIC DESIGN:\n  Architect writes RULES (the parameter set).\n  The computer COMPUTES the geometry from the rules.\n  Want to change window width: change the parameter.\n  The geometry regenerates automatically.\n  The drawing is the OUTPUT of the parameter set."
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CONTEMPORARY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "09-CONTEMPORARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:architecture-history:09-contemporary, git-history:architecture-history:09-contemporary]",
        "canonical_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
        "concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "current_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:architecture-history:contemporary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "architecture-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "section": "architecture-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLE: Parametric Facade\n  RULE SET:\n    Base grid: 1.2m × 3m panels\n    Each panel: rotation angle = f(solar angle, month, hour)\n    Each panel: opacity = g(occupant density at that floor)\n    Panel color: lerp(light, dark) based on floor level\n  RESULT:\n    3000-panel facade where each panel is uniquely positioned\n    based on performance rules, not aesthetic decisions.\n    Change the latitude → regenerate for different solar angle.\n    Change the occupancy program → regenerate for new density.\n    The design IS the parameter set. The geometry is computed."
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CONTEMPORARY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "09-CONTEMPORARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:architecture-history:09-contemporary, git-history:architecture-history:09-contemporary]",
        "canonical_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
