        "root_concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "section": "architecture-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TOPOLOGY OPTIMIZATION:\n  Start with a full block of material (the design space).\n  Apply loads and boundary conditions.\n  Run finite element analysis (FEM).\n  Remove material from elements with low stress.\n  Re-analyze the reduced geometry.\n  Repeat iteratively until target stiffness/weight achieved.\n  Result: organic branching structure that looks like bone,\n    coral, or tree roots — because it IS the same math\n    that nature uses (bones optimize under stress as you grow)."
    },
