        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "2D CAD (pre-BIM):\n  Drawing is lines on paper (or screen).\n  A window is drawn as four lines.\n  No information about what kind of window it is.\n  Change window type: redraw, update sections, update details,\n    update schedules — all manually.\n  Clash detection: print drawings, overlay, look."
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CONTEMPORARY.md#026",
      "path": [
        "09-CONTEMPORARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:architecture-history:09-contemporary, git-history:architecture-history:09-contemporary]",
        "canonical_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
        "concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "current_path": "architecture-history/09-CONTEMPORARY.md",
        "id": "maxim:architecture-history:contemporary",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "architecture-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[contemporary]",
        "section": "architecture-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "3D BIM (Revit, Archicad, Bentley):\n  Every element is a parametric OBJECT with:\n    Geometry: 3D form that appears in plan, section, 3D view\n    Data: manufacturer, model number, cost, U-value, fire rating,\n          maintenance interval, warranty expiry, etc.\n  A window is a BIM object with geometry AND data.\n  Change window type: change the object type.\n    Plan view updates. Section updates. Schedule updates.\n    Cost estimate updates. Energy model updates."
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CONTEMPORARY.md#027",
      "path": [
        "09-CONTEMPORARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:architecture-history:09-contemporary, git-history:architecture-history:09-contemporary]",
