        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Contemporary Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BIM LEVELS (UK Government definition, now partly obsolete):\n  Level 0: 2D CAD only, paper drawings\n  Level 1: 3D CAD, no data, no collaboration\n  Level 2: 3D parametric BIM, file-based collaboration,\n           each discipline manages its own model\n           (UK Government mandate: 2016 for public projects)\n  Level 3: Single federated model, all disciplines in one\n           shared model, cloud-based, live collaboration\n           (still partially aspirational, 2026)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-CONTEMPORARY.md#029",
      "path": [
        "09-CONTEMPORARY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
